  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Unitaid 2023</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Norway is one of Unitaid&apos;s founders. Unitaid  is a global health agency engaged in finding innovative solutions to prevent, diagnose and treat diseases more quickly, affordably, and effectively, in low- and middle-income countries (LMICs). Unitaid&#x2019;s investments address major diseases such as HIV/AIDS, malaria and tuberculosis, as well as HIV co-infections and co-morbidities. Unitaid also works in the fields of cervical cancer, fever management and reproductive, maternal and child health (RMNCH). Unitaid is hosted by the World Health Organization.
Unitaid has been applying its expertise to address challenges in advancing new therapies and diagnostics for the COVID-19 pandemic, serving as a key member of the Access to COVID Tools Accelerator (ACT-A), co-leading the ACT-A Therapeutics Pillar, including the Oxygen Taskforce, and the market readiness workstream of the ACT-A Diagnostics pillar.</narrative>
  </description>
